  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Introducing waste gasification for electricity generation to Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because the project partners have decided to withdraw the project.The applicant, Advanced Processes Inc., is an American firm established in 1998, employing fifteen staff. Advanced Processes Inc. is specialised in waste processing and electricity generation. The local partner Caltech Ventures, is a Ghanaian firm established in 2005. Currently, Caltech grows cassava for production of cassava flour but in the near future also for production of ethanol. Caltech owns 3,400 ha of land of which 250 ha has been planted with cassava.The partners plan to generate renewable energy from cassava waste and municipal waste in the Volta region. The partners will set up a joint venture with equal shareholding and will establish a 600 kW waste to energy plant. The power produced by the joint venture will be sold to the national electricity provider and to Caltech. This will be the first gasification plant in Ghana. Cassava waste will be collected from cassava farmers and municipal waste will be sorted and briquetted at the local landfill site. The electricity off take is guaranteed by the Public Utility and by the local partner. Fertiliser pellets will be produced as a by-product and will be sold to Caltech and other agro-communities.</narrative>
  </description>
